  "id": "u01-l04",
  "unit": "u01-basics",
  "title": "How are you?",
  "tip": "**আছ-** (*achh-*) means 'to be (in a state / somewhere)'. Its ending changes with the person:\n\n- আমি **আছি** (*achhi*) — I am\n- তুমি **আছো** (*achho*) — you (familiar) are\n- আপনি **আছেন** (*achhen*) — you (polite) are\n\nPolite আপনি forms almost always end in **-েন** (*-en*). So: **কেমন আছেন?** (polite) vs **কেমন আছো?** (familiar). The pronoun is often dropped because the ending already says who you mean.\n\nIn Bangladesh many people begin their answer with **আলহামদুলিল্লাহ** ('praise be to God'): *Alhamdulillah, bhalo achhi.*",
  "vocab": [
    { "id": "kemon", "bn": "কেমন", "tr": "kemon", "en": "how" },
    { "id": "achhen", "bn": "আছেন", "tr": "achhen", "en": "are (polite)", "notes": "Goes with আপনি." },
    { "id": "achho", "bn": "আছো", "tr": "achho", "en": "are (familiar)", "notes": "Goes with তুমি. Also spelled আছ; pronounced the same." },
    { "id": "achhi", "bn": "আছি", "tr": "achhi", "en": "am", "notes": "Goes with আমি." },
    { "id": "bhalo", "bn": "ভালো", "tr": "bhalo", "en": "good, well", "notes": "Also spelled ভাল." },
    { "id": "khub", "bn": "খুব", "tr": "khub", "en": "very" },
    { "id": "ar", "bn": "আর", "tr": "ar", "en": "and", "notes": "আর আপনি? = 'And you?'. Also means 'more' / 'else'." },
    { "id": "alhamdulillah", "bn": "আলহামদুলিল্লাহ", "tr": "alhamdulillah", "en": "praise be to God", "notes": "Arabic phrase used very widely by Muslims in Bangladesh, e.g. in answer to 'How are you?'. Hindus and most Kolkata speakers simply say ভালো আছি." }
